==Old Norse==
{{was fwotd|non|2014|June|6}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|non|/ˈstoːlː/|a=12th century Icelandic}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*stōlaz|t=stool, chair, throne}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|stōl}}, {{cog|ofs|stōl}}, {{cog|osx|stōl}}, {{cog|odt|stuol}}, {{cog|goh|stuol}}, {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐍉𐌻𐍃}}. Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*stāl-|t=frame, rack, stand}}. The second meaning is a calque of {{cog|la|sēdēs|t=seat}}, while the third is presumably a calque of {{cog|la|thronī|t=the Thrones}}.

====Noun====
{{non-noun|m|stóls|stólar}}

# a [[stool]], [[chair]], [[throne]]
#* ''[[w:Hákonar_saga_Hákonarsonar|Hákonar saga Hákonarsonar]]'' 254, in '''1835''', [[w:Finnur_Magnússon|F. Magnússon]], [[w:Carl_Christian_Rafn|C. C. Rafn]], ''Fornmanna sögur'', Volume X. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=Wy8IAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA16 16]:
#*: {{...}} þar tvískipat eptir endilöngu, voru skipaðir XIII '''stólar'''.
#*: {{...}} ''there along the entire length [of the king's court] were set in two thirteen '''chairs'''.''
# {{lb|non|ecclesiastic}} [[bishop|bishop's]] [[residence]], [[see]]
#* ''Guðmundar saga'' 68, in '''1858''', [[w:Jón_Sigurðsson|J. Sigurðsson]], [[w:Guðbrandur_Vigfússon|G. Vigfússon]], ''Biskupa sögur'', Volume I. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=py4PAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA508 508]:
#*: {{...}} ok fór hann heim til '''stóls''' sins; {{...}}
#*: {{...}} ''and came back to [the bishop's] '''see''';'' {{...}}
# {{lb|non|Christianity, in the plural}} the [[throne|Thrones]] (a [[class]] of [[angel]]s)
#* ''[[w:Old_Norwegian_Homily_Book|Old Norwegian Homily Book]]'', in '''1864''', C. R. Unger, ''Gammel Norsk Homiliebog''. Christiania, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=oWUAAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA185 185], lines 11-12:
#*: {{...}} þat ero englar oc hofuðenglar oc craftar, veldisenglar oc hofðingiar, drotnar oc '''stolar''', {{...}}
#*: {{...}} ''there are angels and archangels and Powers, Virtues and Principalities, Dominions and '''Thrones''','' {{...}}

